2017-11-21 18:18 GMT+03:00 Remo Dentato <rdentato@gmail.com>:

> Let me say it again (since it seems that my comments usually don't get any
> form of reply).
>
> The key point is that we have tons of people DISCUSSING ABOUT the language
> and very few people actually USING it.
>
> What is worse is that the migration to MediaWiki broke most of the links
> to existing material (e.g. this is one of my translations, try to link on
> the PDF file! https://mw.lojban.org/papri/File:lenumakfaprami.pdf ),
> probably discouraging people to contribute with more material.
>


Simpy download it and open in some pdf reader. i have no idea why Chrome
doesn't want to render it.


> The only way, to me, to make the language evolve is to actually doing
> something with it. The key points, imho, that make Lojban and should never
> be abandonded are:
>
>  - Statement as relation (as opposed to Subject/Verb/objects)
>  - Formal grammar to resolve any parsing ambiguity (I really welcomed
> moving to PEG).
>

Why did you welcome PEG?


>
> mu'e mi'e la .remod.
>
>
>
> On Tue, Nov 21, 2017 at 3:26 PM, <sukender1@gmail.com> wrote:
>
>>
>>>
>>>>    1. Anyone authenticated (= registered somewhere) can create a draft
>>>>    and discuss about existing ones.
>>>>
>>>>
